{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimitRadicalDescent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimitRadicalDescent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimitNotFaithful"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimitRadicalDescent.not_isFaithful_of_orthogonal_H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimitRadicalDescent.not_isFaithful_of_orthogonal_H","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimitRadicalDescent.lean#L85-L91","doc":"The same statement as a non-faithfulness criterion: a nonzero element of one\nlevel, invisible within that level, refutes faithfulness of `trLim`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimitRadicalDescent.mem_rad_of_orthogonal_H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimitRadicalDescent.mem_rad_of_orthogonal_H","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeColimitRadicalDescent.lean#L63-L83","doc":"**Orthogonality at one level is radical membership — unconditionally.**\n\nIf `a` sits at level `k ≥ 1` of the Hecke colimit and the Ocneanu trace form\ncannot see it *within that level*, then it cannot see it anywhere: `a` is in the\nradical of `trLim`.\n\nThis is the conclusion of `QBeta.TLTowerRadicalDescent.map_mem_traceRadical`\nwithout its `HeckeConditionalExpectation` hypothesis.  `TowerSpan` does the work\ninstead, and the Hecke colimit has a `TowerSpan` instance\n(`towerSpan_heckeColimit`, proved from the braid relations). ","signatureChunk":0}]}